      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Upper gastrointestinal hemorrhage is not uncommonly seen by the surgical practitioner. We present a case of a patient who presented with melena and syncope, who was subsequently found to have invasive metastatic pancreatic cancer as his source of bleed."},
